IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gdpr-core`
IMPORT `gdpr-core-2`
IMPORT `gdpr-definitions-2`

-- ============================================================================
-- P2-art-19.l4 -- ARTICLE 19 OF REGULATION (EU) 2016/679: NOTIFICATION OBLIGATION REGARDING RECTIFICATION OR ERASURE OF
-- PERSONAL DATA OR RESTRICTION OF PROCESSING (layer 1).
-- Written by P2 (Sonnet 5.5).  Lines 250-252 of eu-gdpr-2016-679-consolidated-20160504.txt (the two heading lines of
-- Article 19 at 250-251 are `inert` headings).
-- Target compiler: main (build 1.6.112).  Answers: MAYBE `Duty outcome`; a DEONTIC for each regulative rule.
-- WHOSE.  The controller owes the communication to each recipient and the information to the data subject (the data
-- subject's claim: "if the data subject requests it").  This module CALLS the keel: `Art 4(9) the body is a recipient`
-- (gdpr-definitions-2.l4) decides who is a recipient.  Article 19 is among "Articles 15 to 20", so both decision functions
-- (the first and the second sentence) and the regulative rule of the second sentence take P1's answer
-- `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` (see P2-art-15.l4; the second sentence gained it in the fix round, R9).
-- ============================================================================

DECLARE `Art 19 action` IS ONE OF
    `Art 19 communicate the rectification, erasure or restriction of processing to each recipient to whom the personal data have been disclosed`
    `Art 19 inform the data subject about those recipients`

§ `Article 19, first sentence: communicating the change to each recipient`

-- src:252 | The controller shall communicate any rectification or erasure of personal data or restriction of processing carried out in accordance with Article 16, Article 17(1) and Article 18 to each recipient to whom the personal data have been disclosed, unless this proves impossible or involves disproportionate effort.
@ref Art 19 first sentence (src:252)
GIVEN `a rectification, erasure or restriction of processing has been carried out in accordance with Article 16, Article 17(1) or Article 18` IS A BOOLEAN
      body IS A `Kind of person or body`
      `the personal data have been disclosed to the body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a third party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the personal data are received in the framework of a particular inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the receipt is in accordance with Union or Member State law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `communicating it proves impossible or involves disproportionate effort` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the controller has communicated it to the body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
`Art 19 the controller communicates any rectification, erasure or restriction of processing to each recipient to whom the personal data have been disclosed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST `the duty does not arise`
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, Article 11(2)): "Articles 15 to 20 shall not apply except where the data subject"
        IF NOT (`a rectification, erasure or restriction of processing has been carried out in accordance with Article 16, Article 17(1) or Article 18`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any rectification or erasure of personal data or restriction of processing carried out in accordance with Article 16, Article 17(1) and Article 18": with none carried out there is nothing to communicate, and the sentence has no gate word
        IF `Art 4(9) the body is a recipient` body `the personal data have been disclosed to the body` `the body is a third party` `the personal data are received in the framework of a particular inquiry` `the receipt is in accordance with Union or Member State law` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the body is a recipient is the keel's answer (`Art 4(9)`), and it does not answer on these facts
        IF `Art 4(9) the body is a recipient` body `the personal data have been disclosed to the body` `the body is a third party` `the personal data are received in the framework of a particular inquiry` `the receipt is in accordance with Union or Member State law` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to each recipient to whom the personal data have been disclosed": a body that is not a recipient is outside the sentence, and the text does not say no to it in its own words
        IF `communicating it proves impossible or involves disproportionate effort`
        THEN JUST `the duty does not arise`
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "unless"): "unless this proves impossible or involves disproportionate effort"
        IF `the controller has communicated it to the body`
        THEN JUST `the duty arises and is met`
        OTHERWISE JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
        -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question, split site (i)): "The controller shall communicate any rectification or erasure of personal data or restriction of processing ... to each recipient to whom the personal data have been disclosed"

GIVEN `the duty to communicate arises for the recipient` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Role in the Regulation` `Art 19 action`
`Art 19 the controller must communicate the rectification, erasure or restriction of processing to each recipient` MEANS
    IF `the duty to communicate arises for the recipient`
    THEN PARTY controller
         MUST `Art 19 communicate the rectification, erasure or restriction of processing to each recipient to whom the personal data have been disclosed`
    ELSE FULFILLED
    -- no time limit and no consequence is stated (NOTES, Rules with no breach path); the gate is the answer `the duty arises and is met` or `the duty arises and is not met` of the function above, stated by the caller

§ `Article 19, second sentence: informing the data subject about the recipients`

-- src:252 | The controller shall inform the data subject about those recipients if the data subject requests it.
@ref Art 19 second sentence (src:252)
GIVEN `the data subject requests to be informed about those recipients` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the controller informed the data subject about those recipients` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
`Art 19 the controller informs the data subject about those recipients if the data subject requests it` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST `the duty does not arise`
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, Article 11(2)): "Articles 15 to 20 shall not apply except where the data subject" (Article 19 is among Articles 15 to 20; R9)
        IF NOT (`the data subject requests to be informed about those recipients`)
        THEN JUST `the duty does not arise`
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "if", the text says no in its own words): "if the data subject requests it"
        IF `the controller informed the data subject about those recipients`
        THEN JUST `the duty arises and is met`
        OTHERWISE JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
        -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question, split site (i)): "The controller shall inform the data subject about those recipients"

GIVEN `the data subject requests to be informed about those recipients` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Role in the Regulation` `Art 19 action`
`Art 19 the controller must inform the data subject about those recipients if the data subject requests it` MEANS
    IF `the data subject requests to be informed about those recipients` AND NOT (`Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN PARTY controller
         MUST `Art 19 inform the data subject about those recipients`
    ELSE FULFILLED
    -- no time limit and no consequence is stated (NOTES, Rules with no breach path)
